 "frozen_rules": "G (roll12cancel) replaces S as the arithmetic default if G has 0 wrong and G solved >= S solved - 2 (noise band; the owner rule prefers the generic policy). GI (roll12idle) then replaces G if GI has 0 wrong, GI solved >= G solved, at least 1 case is answered by a slot >= 12, and GI arm wall <= 1.10 x G arm wall.",
 "disclosure": "Weaknesses that remain in arms.py-driven arms (arms.py is pinned; disclose in reports): flush_caches ignores the ssh exit status and the HTTP status (only the response text is recorded), delta() accepts negative deltas after a counter reset, parse() counts a missing counter as 0 and accepts non-finite values, wait_idle() returns a busy snapshot after its limit without failing, and an energy failure does not change the exit code.",
 "design_disclosure": "Design notes: (1) escalation agents run on the node of the agent whose end freed their slot, so the same slot can run on different nodes in different arms; (2) each request's sampling seed hashes the agent seed, stage and prompt token ids, so S (hinted prompts) and G/GI (no hints) sample differently for escalation agents even with equal agent seeds, while G and GI share slots 0-11 exactly in seeds and prompts; (3) GI's extra agents depend on node occupancy in the shared slots (agents + judges of all cases of the arm), i.e. on the arm's own load, never on elapsed time; (4) the plan's code_sha256 pins are records checked by review, not enforced by the runner; arms.py must be given --source for the worker revision."
